To simplify \\(\\sqrt{32670}\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Factorize the number 32670 into its prime factors.**\n2. **Use the prime factorization to simplify the square root.**\n\nLet's start with the factorization:\n\n1. **Divide by 2:**\n   \\[\n   32670 \\div 2 = 16335\n   \\]\n   So, \\(32670 = 2 \\times 16335\\).\n\n2. **Divide by 3:**\n   \\[\n   16335 \\div 3 = 5445\n   \\]\n   So, \\(16335 = 3 \\times 5445\\), and thus \\(32670 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 5445\\).\n\n3. **Divide by 3 again:**\n   \\[\n   5445 \\div 3 = 1815\n   \\]\n   So, \\(5445 = 3 \\times 1815\\), and thus \\(32670 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 1815\\).\n\n4. **Divide by 3 again:**\n   \\[\n   1815 \\div 3 = 605\n   \\]\n   So, \\(1815 = 3 \\times 605\\), and thus \\(32670 = 2 \\times 3^3 \\times 605\\).\n\n5. **Factorize 605:**\n   \\[\n   605 \\div 5 = 121\n   \\]\n   So, \\(605 = 5 \\times 121\\), and thus \\(32670 = 2 \\times 3^3 \\times 5 \\times 121\\).\n\n6. **Factorize 121:**\n   \\[\n   121 = 11 \\times 11\n   \\]\n   So, \\(121 = 11^2\\), and thus \\(32670 = 2 \\times 3^3 \\times 5 \\times 11^2\\).\n\nNow we have the prime factorization of 32670:\n\\[\n32670 = 2 \\times 3^3 \\times 5 \\times 11^2\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the prime factorization to simplify the square root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{32670} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 3^3 \\times 5 \\times 11^2}\n\\]\n\nWe can separate the square root into parts that are perfect squares and parts that are not:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{32670} = \\sqrt{2 \\times 3^2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 11^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 \\times 11^2 \\times 2 \\times 3 \\times 5}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\sqrt{3^2} = 3\\) and \\(\\sqrt{11^2} = 11\\), we can take these out of the square root:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{32670} = 3 \\times 11 \\times \\sqrt{2 \\times 3 \\times 5}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[\n2 \\times 3 \\times 5 = 30\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{32670} = 33 \\sqrt{30}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of \\(\\sqrt{32670}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{33\\sqrt{30}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{33\\sqrt{30}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:568"}
